  'tshwane-overnight-restrictions-garsfontein-klapperkop-2026-10-26',
  'Tshwane shuts off water overnight to save low Garsfontein, Klapperkop reservoirs',
  'Utilities', '2026-10-26', 'Rekord (The Citizen)',
  'https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/uncategorized/2026/10/26/low-reservoir-levels-delay-water-recovery-in-garsfontein-and-klapperkop/',
  'The City of Tshwane says critically low reservoirs in Garsfontein and Klapperkop are still delaying supply, leaving some customers dry on 26 October.',
  'The City of Tshwane says reservoir levels feeding the Garsfontein and Klapperkop systems remain critically low, with some customers in those areas still without water. Metro spokesperson Lindela Mashigo said heavy use in suburbs that still have supply is slowing the recovery of the reservoirs that feed areas further down the network. Elardus Park depends on pumps that need adequate reservoir levels to push water to higher ground, while Parkmore and Waverley have seen supply trickle back but remain uneven, with some customers still reporting low pressure or interruptions.

Mashigo said the metro is working with Rand Water to stabilise the system, which has been under strain for weeks. Rand Water announced on 23 October that it would cut bulk supply to municipalities that keep exceeding their allocations, naming Tshwane and Johannesburg among the main offenders. It put the metro''s September consumption at 893 million litres daily, well above its 752-million-litre allocation, and warned the system is still badly strained even before peak summer demand arrives.

Residents in the affected systems are being asked to use water only for essential needs, and to avoid watering gardens, washing cars or filling pools until supply recovers. Customers whose taps are still running are urged to cut back so reservoirs can refill for areas with no water at all. The city says regional teams will send water tankers to the hardest-hit communities, and ward councillors will publish the collection points as they are confirmed.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/uncategorized/2026/10/26/low-reservoir-levels-delay-water-recovery-in-garsfontein-and-klapperkop/", "https://mg.co.za/the-green-guardian/2026-10-23-rand-water-to-restrict-water-supply-to-johannesburg-and-tshwane/"]',
  'agent'
);

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news (
  slug, title, category, published_date, source_name, source_url,
  summary, body, image_url, image_credit, image_source, verification_json, source
) VALUES (
  'tshwane-aid-salvokop-shack-fire-2026-10-26',
  'Tshwane and aid groups rally for families after Salvokop shack fire kills one',
  'Community', '2026-10-26', 'Rekord (The Citizen)',
  'https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/news-headlines/2026/10/26/government-and-organisation-tackle-aftermath-of-informal-settlement-fire/',
  'A weekend fire destroyed about 100 shacks in the Bagdad settlement in Salvokop and killed one resident, leaving 187 people needing emergency help.',
  'A fire over the weekend tore through the Bagdad informal settlement in Salvokop, Pretoria West, destroying an estimated 100 shacks and killing one resident. The City of Tshwane says 187 people, including 10 children, were left needing help. Human Settlements MMC Aaron Maluleka and Community and Social Development MMC Palesa Modise visited the site to assess the damage and coordinate the response, and the city extended condolences to the family of the person who died.

The city''s disaster management unit has handed out 50 mattresses, and its Department of Community and Social Development arranged cooked meals for residents on the day of the fire and the day after. A municipal food bank was due to be activated once officials had assessed household needs. Gift of the Givers has committed 130 hygiene packs, cooked meals and 260 mattresses and blankets between them, the Laudium PMT Burial Society is also handing out meals, and a nearby church is arranging temporary shelter for residents who lost their homes.

Maluleka urged residents, particularly in densely built informal settlements, to take extra care with open flames, candles and electrical appliances to prevent further fires. The city says it will keep working with residents and humanitarian partners in the days ahead as affected families begin rebuilding.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/news-headlines/2026/10/26/government-and-organisation-tackle-aftermath-of-informal-settlement-fire/", "https://iol.co.za/news/politics/2026-10-25-update-tshwane-mobilises-emergency-aid-after-salvokop-fire-destroys-100-shacks-kills-one/"]',
  'agent'
);
